    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="1053" n="1039" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg1039"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856E.00/8–1847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in the
                        United Kingdom </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-20T18:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3591. Dutch requested that US ConGen be directed participate in joint report on
                    situation Indonesia with other career Consuls Batavia (urtel 4464, Aug 18<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d839-f1"/>). Dept replying that in desire to be helpful is
                    willing for ConGen to join with other career consuls in report but recognizes
                    that arrangements for such report will require careful consideration and must be
                    agreeable both Indos and Dutch.</p>
                <p>Sent London as 3591. Repeated Hague as 426, Batavia as 230 and New York as
                    366.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d839-f1" n="3" xml:id="d839-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported a similar request to the British (856E.00/8–1847).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
